      "code": "if (err & PARSE_ERR_TOOMANY) {\n    ha_alert(\"parsing [%s:%d]: too many words, truncating at word %d, position %ld: <%s>.\\n\",\n             file, linenum, MAX_LINE_ARGS, (long)(args[MAX_LINE_ARGS-1] - outline + 1), args[MAX_LINE_ARGS-1]);\n    err_code |= ERR_ALERT | ERR_FATAL;\n    fatal++;\n    goto next_line;\n}",
      "note": "Root cause. When `parse_line()` returns both `PARSE_ERR_TOOMANY` and `PARSE_ERR_TOOLARGE`, `readcfgfile()` takes this branch before the later `if (err & (PARSE_ERR_TOOLARGE|PARSE_ERR_OVERLAP))` block that would resize `outline` to `outlen`. It therefore computes and formats `args[MAX_LINE_ARGS-1]` while that pointer still lies beyond the current `outline` allocation. The staged patch fixes the bug by moving this whole `PARSE_ERR_TOOMANY` block below the allocation-retry branch.",
